#
# This alone only makes GitHub auto-request @joshbain01 as a reviewer on every
# PR — it does NOT block merging without an approval. To make review actually
# *required* (not just requested), enable branch protection on `main`:
#
#   Settings → Branches → Add branch protection rule → branch name pattern "main"
#     [x] Require a pull request before merging
#         [x] Require approvals (at least 1)
#         [x] Require review from Code Owners
#     [x] Do not allow bypassing the above settings (so even an admin/owner
#         push can't skip review — remove this if you want yourself exempt)
#
# Any automation in this repo that opens PRs (e.g. a self-improvement/agentic
# loop) must never approve or merge its own PRs — only a human review counts.

